# V2-10 (b) the open lands on huge planets, each at its heart (`biome=`, `:T` a mean below T °C)
# or at a place (`x=`, `z=`): the Palearctic steppe of seed 7 in summer and under the winter's
# snow; the Nearctic prairie of seed 4 (seed 7 has no dry land in the Nearctic) looking out over
# the lowland and along its plateau; the cold desert in summer and winter; the Old World's hot
# desert and its dunes; the Nearctic hot desert of seed 9; then their animals, close. Seasons
# are the place's own (`season=`, `@` how far into it).
# `hearth --screenshot-list tools/shots/v210_dry.shots`
defaults: seed=7, planet=huge, res=256, w=960, h=540, dist=8, hour=11, clouds=0.25, dry=true
